# 1 Definitions

For purposes of this Agreement, the following terms have the meanings set out below.

## 1.1 Agreement

"Agreement" means this Hi3D Open License Agreement Version 1.0 issued with the applicable version of the Hi3D Materials, including Schedule 1, Acceptable Use Policy, and Schedule 2, Licensed Asset Schedule.

## 1.2 Licensor

"Licensor," "we," "us" or "our" means OCEANO HK HOLDING LIMITED, solely to the extent that it owns or is authorized to license the relevant rights in the Hi3D Materials.

## 1.3 You

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this Agreement. A "legal entity" includes the entity acting hereunder and any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with it. "Control" means direct or indirect ownership of more than fifty percent of the voting interests, or the power to direct management.

## 1.4 Hi3D Materials

"Hi3D Materials" means the source code, model architecture, model weights and parameters, inference code, documentation and other materials that are owned by or licensable by the Licensor and expressly identified in the specific release listed in Schedule 2 as being subject to this Agreement. An asset is not automatically included in this Agreement merely because it has a similar name or purpose or is stored in the same repository, unless it has actually been released and is listed in Schedule 2.

## 1.5 Excluded Materials

"Excluded Materials" means third-party software, models, weights and their outputs; training, validation and test datasets; sample media, fonts and other third-party assets; first-stage systems or server-side code not listed in Schedule 2; trademarks and brand assets except as expressly permitted under Section 8; and any other items expressly subject to separate terms. Excluded Materials are not licensed under this Agreement. Sample code calling a third-party model does not alter the licensing status of that third-party model or its outputs.

## 1.6 Model Derivative

"Model Derivative" means another machine-learning model created by modifying, fine-tuning, adapting or quantizing all or a substantial part of the Hi3D model weights or parameters, or otherwise based on or incorporating the foregoing. Standalone Outputs, including generated 3D meshes and model files and finished works created by editing, converting or combining such files, do not become Model Derivatives merely because they were generated or post-processed; however, any portion of a finished work that actually contains Hi3D code, weights or parameters remains subject to this Agreement according to its nature.

## 1.7 Output

"Output" means content or information generated by running the Hi3D Materials or a Model Derivative, including generated 3D geometry, meshes and exported 3D files. Any third-party asset actually contained in an Output remains subject to the applicable third-party rights or separate license.

## 1.8 Commercial Product or Service

"Commercial Product or Service" means any product, service or hosted functionality that uses or contains the Hi3D Materials or a Model Derivative and is offered for commercial advantage, monetary consideration, revenue generation or other material commercial benefit.

## 1.9 Related Product or Service

"Related Product or Service" means a product or service that uses or contains the Hi3D Materials or a Model Derivative. Substantially similar services split among different brands, applications, interfaces, domain names or affiliated entities to evade the Scale Threshold must be aggregated.

## 1.10 Monthly Active Users

"Monthly Active Users" or "MAU" means the number of unique natural persons who actively use a Related Product or Service during a calendar month.

## 1.11 First Stage

"First Stage" means coarse-mesh generation that generates the basic three-dimensional shape of an object from a reference image, determines its principal structure and approximate contours, and outputs a coarse mesh for subsequent processing.

## 1.12 Second Stage

"Second Stage" means geometry refinement that takes a reference image and the coarse mesh produced by the First Stage as inputs, progressively refines the three-dimensional shape, and generates higher-resolution three-dimensional geometry and mesh files.

