Subject to your continuing compliance with this Agreement, and solely with respect to rights in the Hi3D Materials that the Licensor owns or is authorized to license, the Licensor grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, reproduce, modify, fine-tune and adapt the Hi3D Materials in source-code, object-code, weight or other applicable form; create Model Derivatives and other derivative works; publicly display and publicly perform them; and distribute, sublicense and sell the Hi3D Materials. You may also deploy the Hi3D Materials on servers, cloud platforms or other computing environments that you control or lawfully use, and provide third parties with hosted services based on the Hi3D Materials through websites, applications, application programming interfaces (APIs), software as a service (SaaS) or other remote-access methods. This license may be transferred only through sublicensing or distribution that complies with this Agreement.

## 2.1 Commercial Use

Commercial use is permitted subject to Sections 5, 6, 7 and 8. No revenue threshold applies separately from Section 5.

## 2.2 Training Other AI Models

To the extent the Licensor has the right to grant such permission, you may use the Hi3D Materials and their Outputs to train, evaluate, improve or develop other artificial-intelligence or machine-learning models, subject to applicable law, third-party rights and Schedule 1. This permission does not extend to coarse models, outputs or other third-party materials generated through third-party models, and does not replace their separate license terms. Another model is a Model Derivative only if it satisfies the definition in Section 1.6.

