If you institute patent litigation against the Licensor or any contributor alleging that the Hi3D Materials or a contribution directly or contributorily infringes a patent, all patent licenses granted to you under this Agreement for the Hi3D Materials terminate as of the date the claim is filed.

# 4 Distribution and Sublicensing Conditions

You may distribute the Hi3D Materials and Model Derivatives, including as part of a proprietary or closed-source product, only if you comply with all of the following conditions. Merely reproducing, editing, displaying, selling or distributing Outputs that do not contain Hi3D Materials or Model Derivatives is not distribution under this Section, and does not by itself require those Outputs to be accompanied by this Agreement, a NOTICE file or a modification notice.

- Provide each recipient of files containing the Hi3D Materials or a Model Derivative with the full text of this Agreement upon delivery, or a link that provides continuous, free access to the full text of the corresponding version of this Agreement.
- Retain all applicable copyright, patent and attribution notices contained in the Hi3D Materials.
- Prominently identify the files, weights or materials that you modified.
- When distributing files containing the Hi3D Materials or a Model Derivative, include a readable NOTICE file containing the notice specified in Section 8.2 and all applicable original third-party notices and license requirements.
- Ensure that your terms do not restrict recipients from exercising the rights granted under this Agreement in unmodified portions of the Hi3D Materials, and pass the Acceptable Use Policy downstream as an enforceable condition.

## 4.1 Licensing of Model Derivatives

You may apply different terms, including proprietary terms, to your own modifications and to a Model Derivative as a whole; however, the portions that actually reproduce or embed Hi3D code, weights or parameters remain subject to this Agreement, and the applicable attribution, branding, scale and use conditions continue to apply. A finished 3D work containing only Outputs and not the foregoing Hi3D Materials is not subject to this subsection's conditions for Model Derivatives merely because it was generated using Hi3D.

# 5 Scale Threshold and Separate License

The Scale Threshold is triggered if one or more Related Products or Services exceed 200,000 Monthly Active Users in the most recent complete calendar month or generate monthly revenue of at least USD 1,000,000. Except for the anti-circumvention aggregation rule in Section 1.9, only Related Products or Services are counted.

## 5.1 Application

Within sixty days after first triggering the Scale Threshold, you must notify OCEANO HK HOLDING LIMITED and apply for a separate written license. The application must truthfully disclose the applicant, the affected products and services, the MAU calculation methodology, use cases, deployment regions, security measures and any other information reasonably requested by us.

## 5.2 Transition Period

If you submit a complete, truthful and timely application and remain compliant, you may continue your existing use during the sixty-day application period and while both parties are actively negotiating in good faith; however, without our written consent, you may not materially expand the affected use beyond its scale and scope when the Scale Threshold was first exceeded.

## 5.3 Decision on Separate License

A separate license may include fees, branding, reporting, audit, security, service-level or other commercial terms. We may decide, in our sole discretion, whether to grant or deny a separate license. No separate license is effective unless signed by an authorized representative of OCEANO HK HOLDING LIMITED or otherwise expressly confirmed by it in writing.

## 5.4 Failure to Obtain a License

If you fail to apply within the required period, make a materially false statement in an application, or continue the affected use after written denial or after good-faith negotiations end without agreement, your right to continue above-threshold use terminates. Any continuing above-threshold use is unauthorized and constitutes a material breach.

# 6 Acceptable Use Policy

Your use of the Hi3D Materials and Model Derivatives, and your conduct in generating Outputs with them, must comply with Schedule 1, applicable law and third-party rights. This Agreement does not otherwise restrict the ordinary reproduction, editing, display, sale or distribution of Outputs that have been generated and do not contain Hi3D Materials or Model Derivatives; you remain responsible for complying with applicable law and any third-party rights contained in the Outputs. You may not knowingly assist another person in circumventing restrictions on the use of the Hi3D Materials or Model Derivatives.

## 6.1 Policy Version

The version of Schedule 1 accompanying the Hi3D version you receive applies to that version. We may issue a revised policy for later versions. Material revisions do not apply retroactively to prior versions unless you expressly accept them.

# 7 Commercial Branding Display

Any entity integrating the Hi3D Materials or a Model Derivative into a Commercial Product or Service must display "Powered by Hi3D 1.0" clearly and with reasonable prominence. A product with a user interface must display it in the interface, on an About page or in product acknowledgements. An API, SDK, backend or embedded product without a conventional user interface must display it in primary customer-accessible technical documentation, a service description or a legal notice. Where the display location supports a clickable link, the text must link to the official Hi3D website listed in Schedule 2; if a link cannot be provided, the official website address must be stated in the same location or related documentation. Merely obtaining or using a generated 3D Output file does not, by itself, create the branding-display obligation under this Section.

You may use the Licensor's commercial marks only to comply with the branding-display obligation under this Section. This permission may be revoked at any time and does not transfer any rights or constitute the Licensor's endorsement of you or any related product or service. The Licensor may require you in writing to cease using or remove the relevant marks, and you must do so within five (5) business days after receiving the notice. Once the marks have been removed, you will no longer be subject to the corresponding branding-display obligation.

